          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Dalí's Methodology</strong><br>\nDalí employed a method he termed \"paranoiac-critical,\" a spontaneous method of irrational knowledge based on the interpretative critical association of delirious phenomena. He aimed to transform and subvert reality through this process, bringing forth imaginative compositions.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Hollywood and Design Work</strong><br>\nDalí expanded his artistic exploration into film, working with Alfred Hitchcock on the dream sequences for \"Spellbound\" and designing the logo for Chupa Chups lollipops. His flamboyant personality made him a popular figure in both the art world and popular culture.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Dalí Theatre-Museum</strong><br>\nIn his hometown of Figueres, Dalí dedicated much energy to creating the Dalí Theatre-Museum, which houses many of his works. The museum is a testament to his artistic journey and a reflection of his desire to offer an immersive experience into his imaginative world.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
